  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1040 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nAstronomical fall begins at 704 PM CDT Tuesday, and the autumnal \nequinox will coincide with the start of major heat relief for Middle \nTN. A cold front will push through the area late Tuesday into early \nWednesday with scattered showers and storms followed by a much more \ntypical air mass for this time of year. A few of the storms could be \nstrong into Tuesday evening, but we are not looking for a major \nsevere event. Temperatures after the front, Wednesday through next\nweekend, will be mostly in the lower 80s for highs and lower 60s \nfor lows. The Plateau will have mostly 70s and 50s. The cooler air\nwill also come with mostly dry conditions for late week.",
